---
title: Publish flow, persistence, and distribution
date: '2026-06-16'
tags:
  - added
  - changed
summary: Publish flow with public changelog rendering and export, SQLite persistence, an RSS feed, an embeddable widget, and semver inference from conventional commits.
---

GitHerald added an explicit **changelog publish action**. A signed-in user can
review a generated draft, then publish its changelog to the configured app's
public page. Blog and social copy remain drafts for manual copy or export;
this release did not add direct posting or scheduling.

The release also added a SQLite-backed store, Markdown/HTML/JSON export, an RSS
feed, an embeddable changelog view, conventional-commit version inference, and
a minimal `GET /health` endpoint. The AI provider can be selected through
configuration.

The previous paired landing images were archived from this entry because they
advertised an unconnected waitlist, pricing, editing, and publishing behavior
that this product release did not provide. Product UI screenshots and films
for this release still need to be captured and verified.
